>>
Rule 1 (x and y must have identical dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 2 (broadcast-compatibility from x’s perspective)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : if i < ndim(v_2) then (shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) = 1) else shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) = 1
>>
Rule 3 (broadcast-compatibility from y’s perspective)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : if i < ndim(v_1) then (shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) = shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) = 1) else shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) = 1
>>
Rule 4 (if ranks are equal, each aligned dimension must match or be 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 5 (name is an arbitrary string)
{v_1 : str} |= v_1 = "none" ∨ v_1 ≠ "none"
